 "notes": "Spine: need -> DA hypothesis -> chitosan base + DA sweep -> acetylation/deacetylation -> DA (amine/acetamide fraction) -> two branches: (i) crystallinity -> solubility -> lysozyme degradation, bell-shaped; (ii) ammonium charge density -> clustering -> viability/neurite loss. They meet at PRF c18 (low-DA films for nerve guides). The F2 dual curve (with vs without enzyme) is a component partition read by compare_coplotted_quantities. Main audit c31: F4's adhesion series is nearly flat across DA, which weakens the adhesion-mediated mechanism c17 for the ~75-fold viability collapse. The zero-neurite window coincides with the dissolution window (c28 -> c33, correlate_across_series), which suggests surface instability as an alternative or co-cause; the packet text is truncated where the paper may argue this. Lost: Table 1 NMR values (text_only), crystallinity data (not in packet)."
}